think Fourth lap. The prior lap closed the first of three tooling-parity gaps (the X25519 runner). Continuing the kg the prior recommend named: signed_carry, the first composition, is next — provenance is the more foundational of the two remaining (a signed record is the shape Kumara identity, Vault, and the Lotus 'who made this record' carry all reach for before confidentiality).
think Non-gated: the runner builds crypto/signed_carry.rye to the gitignored crypto/bin/ and runs its selftest over a TEST seed — no real identity key, no network, no funds, no device. Sealing a record with the maintainer's own key stays the custody gate; this only re-proves the library over a test seed.
obs GREEN on the first run. Modeled byte-for-shape on tools/crypto_aead_witness.rish and the x25519 runner just landed: three say lines (Language EN · Style Radiant · Lens TAME), then build, selftest to crypto/bin/signed_carry.out, grep the 'GREEN crypto-signed-carry' token (note the token is crypto-signed-carry, not crypto-signed — the earlier survey grep truncated at the hyphen). The signed carry's parity story is unchanged (eight payload lengths, determinism, independent BLAKE2b + primitive-verify cross-check, seven named refusals); this lap adds the runner that re-proves it on demand.
obs One tooling-parity gap remains — sealed_session — the next and final kg lap of this sub-arc, its own signed round. No custody gate touched.
